# ============================================================
# OpenEvolve credentials TEMPLATE - copy to .env and fill in.
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Usage:
#   1. Copy-Item .env.example .env
#   2. Replace the placeholder below with your real API key
#   3. Never commit .env - the repo .gitignore excludes it
#
# ASCII-ONLY ON PURPOSE. run.ps1 reads .env with PowerShell 5.1; non-ASCII bytes
# can be mis-decoded and swallow a line break, which silently drops the key line.
# ============================================================

# The variable name must stay DEEPSEEK_API_KEY even if the gateway changes:
#   - evolve/config.yaml has   api_key: "${DEEPSEEK_API_KEY}"
#   - openevolve only expands ${VAR} for the api_key field
#   - evolve/run.ps1 loads this file into process environment variables
# If the names disagree the run starts with an empty key and fails with 401.
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_REAL_KEY


# ------------------------------------------------------------
# The gateway URL is NOT configured here.
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# api_base lives in evolve/config.yaml (it is not a secret and should be
# versioned). openevolve does not expand env vars in that field.
#
# Current gateway: https://api.toskaxy.xyz/v1
#   - measured 2026-09-23: /v1/models returns exactly one model,
#     deepseek-v4.1-flash
#   - that model is a REASONING model: reasoning_tokens count towards
#     completion_tokens, so config.yaml max_tokens must be generous (16384)
#   - after switching gateways, update api_base and models in config.yaml,
#     then run  .\run.ps1 -DryRun  to list what the endpoint actually serves
